Z||000000||DJRice||01-30-2001||07:38 PM||||Well I am surfing the forum here while Im waiting for my dinner to get ready and It occured to me to find out what all the other guys (or girls) who live by themselves do for dinner.  <P>Tonight I got a bit fancy.  I had some Gortons Skillet Fillet Lemon Butter Fish Fillets with some canned corn.  Last night I threw a bubba burger on the good ole George Foreman Grill.  Ive also been known to throw a chicken breast on the GF grill.  <P>I also like skillet sensations and of course frozen pizzas.  (pizzas are like dinner and breakfast, it doesnt get more efficent than that)  <P>So what do you do for dinner?<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||01-30-2001||07:41 PM||||Hamburgers that I think used to be racoons<BR>Lotsa coke ..no not that kind<BR>salad in a bag<P>I only eat good when Lisa comes up , then I have to cook something edible.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||01-30-2001||07:48 PM||||I live with my GF, but I still eat bachelor style I guess.  Lots of frozen waffles and pancakes.  Cup O Noodles, ramen noodles, macaroni, creamed corn(mmmmmmm good), tofu products, etc...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaft||01-30-2001||07:54 PM||||The GF GRILL IS THE BEST!!! I cook off that constantly. Other than that Chicken Parmasean and BBQ chicken is real easy. (Throw it in the oven...take a shower...pull it out and eat) I also go through a good bit of Hamburger Helper. If you haven't already, throw some Steak-umms on the GF, they cook in about 20 sec. and are REAL good. I throw some cheese on them and occaisionally some BBQ sauce too.||||reg||10
Z||000004||bHooper||01-30-2001||10:00 PM||||well, I'm not single any more... but cooking on the GF grill, or the real gas grill is the way to go!<P>I would always buy those real cheap pieces of meat, like $2 for a 3 pack of pork chops, and dine like a king!<P>The key to being a batchlor is not what you eat, but what you use for a plate... the sink is an excellent substitute for the garbage can, to eat over.  That way you don't have to dirty any dish's!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000005||DrRodey||01-30-2001||10:02 PM||||A box of Hamburger Helper/Chicken Helper is about perfect for My GF and I.  Add a little side salad, and a couple glasses of **fill in alcoholic beverage of choice** maybe a couple candles and you got a fancy meal too....<P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">          <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||01-30-2001||10:27 PM||||My fav batchelor meal is tomato soup and grilled cheese sandwiches. mmmm. When I'm feeling a little more adventurous I like to cook Italian food. Tortellini Alfredo and peppered chicken is my specialty. Gawd, now I'm hungry again, off to the fridge....||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||01-30-2001||10:32 PM||||Hoop, you got that right... minimal dirty dishes is the key. Whenever I stop at a fast food joint, I throw a handful of plastic forks and spoons into the bag. After I use them later on at home, I just throw them away... no more dishpan hands. Paper plates are relatively cheap and worth while investments too. My normal supper speciality is nuking a frozen dinner. However tonight, it was a bag of microwave popcorn and a beer.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Patrick's Dad||01-30-2001||10:40 PM||||I still eat like a bachelor, or, more accurately, like I did when I was younger. Meal of choice: A Fluffernutter! My wife just sighs. I used to wash it down with nothing but Mountain Dew, but these days, it's Arizona Green Tea with Ginseng and Honey. Yum!<P>Unfortunately, lateral growth is a side effect of still eating like that.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||beer_stud_21||01-30-2001||10:55 PM||||Mc Redneck sandwitches at Mc D's with no mayo.(.99)  foot long veggie subway sandwitch (2.99+tax.. cant beat it) Promax protein bars (spendy, but hopfully they will help make my skinny ass buff..  ;-)  Oh, and stock up on those 2lb bag of animal crackers at Wally World.  Oh, and AZ tee with ginsing in the blue glass bottle.  Best non-alcoholic beverage on earth.  You know what ginsing does to you dont you?  "Makes your life hard and you dick long..."  Or was it the other way around?  hehe  ;-) <P>-Marlin||||reg||6
Z||000010||stimpy||01-31-2001||01:55 AM||||Alright, it's gonna take a fat boy to teach y'all how to eat right. I'm talkin tacos! No, not those greasy fast food concoctions with lettuce and cheese. Yech. Nope. Here's the real deal lowdown on some barrio style carne asada from the gringo himself.<BR> Meat- if you got yourself a real carneceria in town, good start. get a half pound of pre-marinated carne asada. If not, have the butcher filet some flank steak for you.<BR>Marinate for at least a couple of hours in marinade of limes, orange juice concentrate (just a little bit) shot of tequila, and chile powder. Cook on an open fire, just searing it both sides. The stuff is thin, so don't go making bacon out of it.<BR> Now, for tortillas. Get white corn tortillas and grill them on the fire. A slight burn is ok, and actually preferable.<BR> On top, take that shredded lettuce and feed it to the goat. Diced onion, jalepenos, maybe tomato, definately cilantro. Mucho chile sauce. If you must use cheese, let it be the white crumbly Mexican cheese.<P>The carne asada taco is good for any meal. Especially good for breakfast the morning after. Your stomach will thank me.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||01-31-2001||02:33 AM||||Microwave Chef Boyardee Lasagna!!!<BR>also Mr. Noodles, cheese & crackers.. and whatever the cafeteria is serving.<BR>I live in residence right now so I don't have to cook for myself yet. I do own a sandwich griller, a crock pot, a coffeemaker, frying pan, pots, etc.. and I'm soon getting a George Foreman grill.. those things ROCK! I used to use my parents grill all the time back at home.<P>I expect I'll be eating a lot of grilled vegetables served over noodles or rice etc.. I'll try to keep some tupperware containers full of sliced vegetables so I can quickly make fresh sandwiches too.<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000012||Philphine||01-31-2001||03:21 AM||||to be in the delivery zone of a good pizza place and a microwave to warm up what you don't eat when you first get it.  ||||reg||1
