Z||000018||Monkeyman||01-31-2001||06:32 PM||||Being another new bachelor means eating cold beans out of a can.  (I never could cook.)  <P>Bill--Email me sometime.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Cheever2||01-31-2001||08:10 PM||||Not a bachelor, but when working nights for years & being alone during the daytime, I got a bag of frozen Italian Meatballs and put 'em in a pan of Hunts Spaghetti Sauce for 30 minutes.  Excellent while watching the noon Eyewitless news.  Or I'd get a couple of T-bone's and grill 'em and eat with A-1 and some cheese.  Maybe a bag o' salad (Ceasar).  If not salad, then a pickle and some of those itty-bitty tomatoes.<P>When I was a real bachelor my friends would come over and ask "Whatchya got in the fridge?"  I'd have to say "Check it out & you tell me".  When I heard "All you got in here is a bottle of water and two slices of cheese", I replied "Make yourself a cheese sandwich".  Then would come "What's this baking soda in here for?", and the answer of course was "Don't want my water to taste like cheese".<BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000020||Jaygee79||02-01-2001||12:15 PM||||Anything that comes in a can or package.  Frozen lasagna's are good.  Tuna Helper is pretty good too.  And I love that salad-in-a-bag.  For normal food I eat at other people's houses  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
